  "rationale": "ROP/GRA sublibrary (376 genes, ~10 gRNAs each, 3,757 guides; no non-targeting guides) of the in vivo Toxoplasma CRISPR study. Virulent RH tachyzoites carrying the sublibrary were passaged in vitro (P3, P4) and in vivo through WT C57BL/6 mice (WT_* ; three independent screens, 20 libraries) and through Ifngr1-/- mice (KO_* ; 7 libraries). In vivo libraries are heavily bottlenecked (top 1% of guides hold 20-40% of reads, ~1,100-1,800 of 3,757 guides zero), so totals use median_ratio and only between-arm comparisons are interpretable. Primary analysis WT vs KO (KO reference) reproduces the paper's Fig 3 / Table S1E: genes depleted in WT but not in Ifngr1-/- mice are IFN-gamma-dependent virulence factors (ROP5, ROP18, GRA12, GRA45). Secondary P4 vs WT (Fig 2 / S1A) gives in vivo fitness in WT mice. No neutral controls (the shared gene panel mixes essential and dispensable genes), so calibration and the control null are not used.",
